Our pharmaceuticals company is currently experiencing issues with overstocking and stockouts of medications, waste due to expired drugs, and inefficiencies in our delivery routes to pharmacies. We've collected detailed data on our current inventory, including the name, quantity, and turnover rate of each product we have in stock, as well as expiration dates. Additionally, we gathered logistics data detailing our existing delivery routes, times, and pharmacy demand patterns across our network.

Here's the inventory data in JSON format containing product quantities and turnover rates:

```json
{
  "inventory": [
    {"product": "Amoxicillin", "quantity": 1500, "turnoverRate": "0.75"},
    {"product": "Metformin", "quantity": 2800, "turnoverRate": "0.59"},
    // ... rest of the inventory data
  ]
}
```

And here's the expiration data in JSON format with drug expiration dates and quantities:

```json
{
  "expiration": [
    {"product": "Amoxicillin", "quantity": 200, "expirationDate": "2023-06-01"},
    {"product": "Metformin", "quantity": 500, "expirationDate": "2023-07-15"},
    // ... rest of the expiration data
  ]
